{"segments": [{"text": "They were told Black men could not fight in tanks. The 761st Tank Battalion answered with 183 days of uninterrupted combat. They were the Black Panthers.", "imageFile": "images/seg_00.jpg", "clipFile": "clips/clip_00.mp4", "clipFrames": 0, "clipNaturalW": 1730, "clipNaturalH": 1920, "audioFile": "audio/seg_00.mp3", "durationInFrames": 320, "wordTimings": [[0.0, 0.2], [0.2, 0.32], [0.32, 0.58], [0.58, 0.9], [0.9, 1.14], [1.14, 1.34], [1.34, 1.62], [1.62, 1.84], [1.84, 2.1], [2.1, 2.48], [3.12, 3.16], [3.16, 4.34], [4.34, 4.5], [4.5, 4.96], [4.96, 5.36], [5.36, 5.76], [5.76, 6.72], [6.72, 7.06], [7.06, 7.4], [7.4, 8.04], [8.04, 8.48], [9.14, 9.4], [9.4, 9.72], [9.72, 9.88], [9.88, 10.14], [10.14, 10.56]], "isMapOrDoc": false, "personName": null, "portraits": [], "overlay": {"cue": "183 days of uninterrupted combat", "kicker": "761ST TANK BATTALION", "label": "DAYS OF UNINTERRUPTED COMBAT", "type": "stat", "value": 183}}, {"text": "This is how they fought across Europe.\n\nActivated in 1942, the battalion trained for nearly two years in the Jim Crow South — Kentucky, Louisiana, Texas.", "imageFile": "images/seg_01.jpg", "clipFile": "clips/clip_01.mp4", "clipFrames": 0, "clipNaturalW": 1920, "clipNaturalH": 1477, "audioFile": "audio/seg_01.mp3", "durationInFrames": 289, "wordTimings": [[0.0, 0.2], [0.2, 0.38], [0.38, 0.46], [0.46, 0.68], [0.68, 0.82], [0.82, 1.14], [1.14, 1.56], [2.14, 2.5], [2.5, 2.76], [2.76, 3.46], [4.12, 4.14], [4.14, 4.54], [4.54, 4.82], [4.82, 4.98], [4.98, 5.24], [5.24, 5.52], [5.52, 5.86], [5.86, 6.06], [6.06, 6.14], [6.14, 6.3], [6.3, 6.6], [6.6, 7.1], [7.1, 7.38], [7.38, 7.72], [8.18, 8.6], [9.26, 9.46]], "isMapOrDoc": false, "personName": null, "portraits": [], "overlay": null}, {"text": "White units shipped overseas after two or three months. The 761st drilled, waited, and drilled again.\n\nThen General George Patton came to review them. He said: \"Men, you're the first Negro tankers to ever fight in the American Army.", "imageFile": "images/seg_02.jpg", "clipFile": "clips/clip_02.mp4", "clipFrames": 0, "clipNaturalW": 1537, "clipNaturalH": 1920, "audioFile": "audio/seg_02.mp3", "durationInFrames": 423, "wordTimings": [[0.0, 0.32], [0.32, 0.64], [0.64, 0.92], [0.92, 1.32], [1.32, 1.72], [1.72, 1.92], [1.92, 1.96], [1.96, 2.18], [2.18, 2.58], [3.14, 3.2], [3.2, 4.12], [4.12, 4.52], [4.9, 5.1], [5.46, 5.6], [5.6, 5.78], [5.78, 6.26], [6.96, 7.18], [7.18, 7.44], [7.44, 7.78], [7.78, 8.18], [8.18, 8.4], [8.4, 8.56], [8.56, 8.74], [8.74, 9.28], [9.5, 9.7], [9.7, 10.08], [10.54, 10.72], [11.16, 11.26], [11.26, 11.38], [11.38, 11.68], [11.68, 12.0], [12.0, 12.5], [12.5, 12.7], [12.7, 12.94], [12.94, 13.16], [13.16, 13.38], [13.38, 13.44], [13.44, 13.7], [13.7, 14.06]], "isMapOrDoc": false, "personName": null, "portraits": [{"file": "images/portrait_02_0.jpg", "name": "George S. Patton", "startFrame": 196, "endFrame": 332, "naturalW": 633, "naturalH": 800}], "overlay": {"type": "wiki-quote", "cue": "came to review them", "article": "761st Tank Battalion (United States)", "highlight": "General George S. Patton reviewed the battalion and made a speech to the men", "image": "wiki/761st_tank_battalion__united_states_02.png"}}, {"text": "I would never have asked for you if you weren't good.\"\n\nOn November 7th, 1944, they entered the line in Lorraine, France, attached to the 26th Infantry Division — often at the very tip of the advance.", "imageFile": "images/seg_03.jpg", "clipFile": "clips/clip_03.mp4", "clipFrames": 240, "clipNaturalW": 398, "clipNaturalH": 324, "audioFile": "audio/seg_03.mp3", "durationInFrames": 330, "wordTimings": [[0.0, 0.18], [0.18, 0.32], [0.32, 0.48], [0.48, 0.7], [0.7, 0.88], [0.88, 1.06], [1.06, 1.2], [1.2, 1.3], [1.3, 1.44], [1.44, 1.62], [1.62, 2.12], [2.56, 2.64], [2.64, 2.88], [2.88, 4.2], [4.2, 4.2], [4.76, 4.92], [4.92, 5.08], [5.08, 5.3], [5.3, 5.54], [5.54, 5.74], [5.74, 6.14], [6.38, 6.74], [6.92, 7.08], [7.08, 7.32], [7.32, 7.44], [7.44, 8.12], [8.12, 8.38], [8.38, 8.86], [8.86, 9.44], [9.44, 9.58], [9.58, 9.8], [9.8, 9.9], [9.9, 10.1], [10.1, 10.28], [10.28, 10.46], [10.46, 10.56], [10.56, 10.92]], "isMapOrDoc": false, "personName": null, "portraits": [], "overlay": null}, {"text": "At Moyenvic, at Vic-sur-Seille, at Morville, the fighting was point-blank and brutal.\n\nNovember alone cost them 156 casualties. Fourteen tanks were knocked out; twenty more were damaged.", "imageFile": "images/seg_04.jpg", "clipFile": "clips/clip_04.mp4", "clipFrames": 240, "clipNaturalW": 468, "clipNaturalH": 360, "audioFile": "audio/seg_04.mp3", "durationInFrames": 381, "wordTimings": [[0.0, 0.3], [0.3, 1.26], [1.26, 1.4], [1.4, 2.6], [2.6, 2.72], [2.72, 3.24], [3.7, 3.76], [3.76, 3.98], [3.98, 4.24], [4.24, 4.82], [4.82, 5.04], [5.04, 5.46], [6.16, 6.36], [6.36, 6.86], [6.86, 7.16], [7.16, 7.56], [7.56, 8.5], [8.5, 9.0], [9.0, 10.06], [10.06, 10.48], [10.48, 10.64], [10.64, 10.82], [10.82, 11.3], [11.3, 11.78], [11.78, 12.06], [12.06, 12.24], [12.24, 12.58]], "isMapOrDoc": false, "personName": null, "portraits": [], "overlay": {"cue": "November alone cost them 156 casualties", "items": [{"label": "CASUALTIES", "value": "156"}, {"label": "TANKS KNOCKED OUT", "value": "14"}, {"label": "TANKS DAMAGED", "value": "20"}], "title": "NOVEMBER 1944 — THE TOLL", "type": "checklist"}}, {"text": "They had been fighting for weeks. They would not be pulled from the line for months.\n\nIn December, the Germans smashed through the Ardennes. The 761st was rushed north to Belgium to relieve the surrounded 101st Airborne at Bastogne.", "imageFile": "images/seg_05.jpg", "clipFile": "clips/clip_05.mp4", "clipFrames": 240, "clipNaturalW": 468, "clipNaturalH": 360, "audioFile": "audio/seg_05.mp3", "durationInFrames": 377, "wordTimings": [[0.0, 0.15], [0.15, 0.3], [0.3, 0.48], [0.48, 0.7], [0.7, 1.04], [1.04, 1.44], [1.94, 2.04], [2.04, 2.22], [2.22, 2.44], [2.44, 2.62], [2.62, 2.78], [2.78, 3.06], [3.06, 3.12], [3.12, 3.3], [3.3, 3.54], [3.54, 4.02], [4.62, 4.7], [4.7, 5.02], [5.18, 5.3], [5.3, 5.56], [5.56, 6.0], [6.0, 6.28], [6.28, 6.44], [6.44, 6.94], [7.44, 7.56], [7.56, 8.46], [8.46, 8.66], [8.66, 8.96], [8.96, 9.22], [9.22, 9.42], [9.42, 9.7], [9.7, 10.02], [10.02, 10.2], [10.2, 10.42], [10.42, 10.76], [10.76, 11.44], [11.44, 11.8], [11.8, 12.04], [12.04, 12.52]], "isMapOrDoc": false, "personName": null, "portraits": [], "overlay": null}, {"text": "At the town of Tillet, with just eleven tanks, they attacked for two straight days alongside the 87th Infantry Division. They lost nine tanks — and they took the town.", "imageFile": "images/seg_06.jpg", "clipFile": "clips/clip_06.mp4", "clipFrames": 207, "clipNaturalW": 492, "clipNaturalH": 360, "audioFile": "audio/seg_06.mp3", "durationInFrames": 289, "wordTimings": [[0.0, 0.22], [0.22, 0.28], [0.28, 0.42], [0.42, 0.6], [0.6, 1.26], [1.26, 1.38], [1.38, 1.76], [1.76, 2.02], [2.02, 2.5], [2.98, 3.06], [3.06, 3.32], [3.32, 3.56], [3.56, 3.84], [3.84, 4.1], [4.1, 4.44], [4.44, 4.88], [4.88, 5.18], [5.18, 5.78], [5.78, 6.04], [6.04, 6.52], [7.1, 7.26], [7.26, 7.48], [7.48, 7.8], [7.8, 8.28], [8.28, 8.82], [8.82, 8.92], [8.92, 9.06], [9.06, 9.16], [9.16, 9.36], [9.36, 9.58]], "isMapOrDoc": false, "personName": null, "portraits": [], "overlay": null}, {"text": "After the Bulge, they smashed through the Siegfried Line itself, tearing open the road that let the 4th Armored Division pour into Germany.\n\nThen came the drive across the Reich — town after town falling to the Black Panthers in an advance the Germans could not stop.", "imageFile": "images/seg_07.jpg", "clipFile": "clips/clip_07.mp4", "clipFrames": 229, "clipNaturalW": 468, "clipNaturalH": 360, "audioFile": "audio/seg_07.mp3", "durationInFrames": 430, "wordTimings": [[0.0, 0.32], [0.32, 0.52], [0.52, 0.92], [1.18, 1.3], [1.3, 1.66], [1.66, 1.92], [1.92, 2.1], [2.1, 2.4], [2.4, 2.7], [2.7, 3.32], [3.64, 3.8], [3.8, 4.08], [4.08, 4.28], [4.28, 4.44], [4.44, 4.6], [4.6, 4.8], [4.8, 4.98], [4.98, 5.220000000000001], [5.220000000000001, 5.46], [5.46, 5.88], [5.88, 6.24], [6.24, 6.54], [6.54, 6.88], [7.62, 7.86], [7.86, 8.04], [8.04, 8.22], [8.22, 8.4], [8.4, 8.72], [8.72, 8.94], [8.94, 9.18], [9.18, 9.78], [9.78, 10.0], [10.0, 10.4], [10.4, 10.78], [10.78, 11.08], [11.08, 11.32], [11.32, 11.4], [11.4, 11.66], [11.66, 12.08], [12.08, 12.34], [12.34, 12.46], [12.46, 12.82], [12.82, 13.1], [13.1, 13.36], [13.36, 13.7], [13.7, 14.0], [14.0, 14.22]], "isMapOrDoc": false, "personName": null, "portraits": [], "overlay": null}, {"text": "On May 4th, 1945, alongside the 71st Infantry Division, they liberated the Gunskirchen concentration camp in Austria — freeing thousands of prisoners the Nazis had left to die.", "imageFile": "images/seg_08.jpg", "clipFile": "clips/clip_08.mp4", "clipFrames": 0, "clipNaturalW": 1920, "clipNaturalH": 1444, "audioFile": "audio/seg_08.mp3", "durationInFrames": 315, "wordTimings": [[0.0, 0.22], [0.22, 0.4], [0.4, 1.6], [1.6, 1.6], [1.94, 2.26], [2.26, 2.58], [2.58, 3.22], [3.22, 3.5], [3.5, 3.96], [4.48, 4.54], [4.54, 4.9], [4.9, 5.16], [5.16, 5.78], [5.78, 6.44], [6.44, 6.76], [6.76, 6.9], [6.9, 7.34], [7.34, 7.84], [7.84, 8.14], [8.14, 8.52], [8.52, 8.72], [8.72, 9.04], [9.04, 9.36], [9.36, 9.6], [9.6, 9.86], [9.86, 10.02], [10.02, 10.28], [10.28, 10.46]], "isMapOrDoc": false, "personName": null, "portraits": [], "overlay": {"cue": "On May 4th, 1945", "date": "4 MAY 1945", "sub": "GUNSKIRCHEN LIBERATED", "type": "date"}}, {"text": "Days later, at Steyr on the Enns River, they met troops of the Soviet Red Army — among the first Americans to do so. 183 days after it began, their war was over.", "imageFile": "images/seg_09.jpg", "clipFile": "clips/clip_09.mp4", "clipFrames": 270, "clipNaturalW": 470, "clipNaturalH": 360, "audioFile": "audio/seg_09.mp3", "durationInFrames": 337, "wordTimings": [[0.0, 0.36], [0.36, 0.74], [0.96, 1.16], [1.16, 1.52], [1.52, 1.76], [1.76, 1.88], [1.88, 2.14], [2.14, 2.44], [2.88, 2.9], [2.9, 3.1], [3.1, 3.36], [3.36, 3.58], [3.58, 3.68], [3.68, 3.96], [3.96, 4.28], [4.28, 4.78], [4.78, 5.12], [5.12, 5.24], [5.24, 5.48], [5.48, 5.72], [5.72, 6.16], [6.16, 6.46], [6.46, 6.64], [6.64, 7.12], [7.94, 8.5], [8.5, 8.86], [8.86, 9.18], [9.18, 9.34], [9.34, 9.72], [10.2, 10.44], [10.44, 10.62], [10.62, 10.94], [10.94, 11.22]], "isMapOrDoc": false, "personName": null, "portraits": [], "overlay": {"type": "wiki-quote", "cue": "they met troops of the Soviet Red Army", "article": "761st Tank Battalion (United States)", "highlight": "the 761st was one of the first American units to reach Steyr, Austria, at the Enns River", "image": "wiki/761st_tank_battalion__united_states_09.png"}}, {"text": "The price was staggering: nearly half the battalion became casualties, and seventy-one tanks were lost. In return, they killed over six thousand German soldiers and captured nearly sixteen thousand more.", "imageFile": "images/seg_10.jpg", "clipFile": "clips/clip_10.mp4", "clipFrames": 240, "clipNaturalW": 468, "clipNaturalH": 360, "audioFile": "audio/seg_10.mp3", "durationInFrames": 354, "wordTimings": [[0.0, 0.2], [0.2, 0.46], [0.46, 0.8], [0.8, 1.2], [1.82, 1.98], [1.98, 2.32], [2.32, 2.44], [2.44, 2.8], [2.8, 3.14], [3.14, 3.62], [4.22, 4.38], [4.38, 4.78], [4.78, 5.2], [5.2, 5.44], [5.44, 5.82], [6.42, 6.54], [6.54, 6.92], [7.16, 7.3], [7.3, 7.48], [7.48, 7.78], [7.78, 8.17], [8.17, 8.56], [8.56, 8.82], [8.82, 9.2], [9.2, 9.78], [9.78, 10.06], [10.06, 10.44], [10.44, 10.95], [10.95, 11.46], [11.46, 11.76]], "isMapOrDoc": false, "personName": null, "portraits": [], "overlay": {"cue": "The price was staggering", "items": [{"label": "TANKS LOST", "value": "71"}, {"label": "GERMANS KILLED", "value": "6,000+"}, {"label": "GERMANS CAPTURED", "value": "16,000"}], "title": "THE PRICE — AND THE TALLY", "type": "checklist"}}, {"text": "Sergeant Ruben Rivers refused to abandon his men after his tank was hit, fighting on until his wounds killed him. Fifty-three years later, America finally awarded him the Medal of Honor.", "imageFile": "images/seg_11.jpg", "clipFile": "clips/clip_11.mp4", "clipFrames": 0, "clipNaturalW": 1582, "clipNaturalH": 1920, "audioFile": "audio/seg_11.mp3", "durationInFrames": 306, "wordTimings": [[0.0, 0.4], [0.4, 0.86], [0.86, 1.18], [1.18, 1.62], [1.62, 1.88], [1.88, 2.08], [2.08, 2.38], [2.38, 2.64], [2.64, 2.88], [2.88, 3.1], [3.1, 3.26], [3.26, 3.5], [3.5, 3.96], [4.24, 4.38], [4.38, 4.74], [4.74, 4.88], [4.88, 5.12], [5.12, 5.34], [5.34, 5.6], [5.6, 6.18], [6.18, 6.8], [6.8, 7.2], [7.2, 7.74], [8.02, 8.26], [8.26, 8.78], [8.78, 9.1], [9.1, 9.42], [9.42, 9.58], [9.58, 9.76], [9.76, 9.98], [9.98, 10.12]], "isMapOrDoc": false, "personName": null, "portraits": [{"file": "images/portrait_11_0.jpg", "name": "Ruben Rivers", "startFrame": 0, "endFrame": 123, "naturalW": 207, "naturalH": 276}], "overlay": {"type": "wiki-quote", "cue": "awarded him the Medal of Honor", "article": "Ruben Rivers", "highlight": "In 1997, he was awarded the Medal of Honor, the nation's highest military decoration for valor", "image": "wiki/ruben_rivers_11.png"}}, {"text": "They came home to prejudice, not parades. Thirty-three years later, in 1978, President Jimmy Carter presented the battalion with its Presidential Unit Citation. 183 days. Four campaigns. A continent crossed. Come out fighting.", "imageFile": "images/seg_12.jpg", "clipFile": "clips/clip_12.mp4", "clipFrames": 0, "clipNaturalW": 1920, "clipNaturalH": 1534, "audioFile": "audio/seg_12.mp3", "durationInFrames": 483, "wordTimings": [[0.0, 0.22], [0.22, 0.38], [0.38, 0.6], [0.6, 0.82], [0.82, 1.22], [1.56, 1.78], [1.78, 2.36], [2.36, 3.28], [3.28, 3.72], [3.72, 3.98], [4.3, 4.3], [4.3, 5.04], [5.72, 5.9], [5.9, 6.24], [6.24, 6.58], [6.58, 6.9], [6.9, 7.1], [7.1, 7.48], [7.48, 7.72], [7.72, 7.96], [7.96, 8.42], [8.42, 8.84], [8.84, 9.38], [10.5, 11.18], [11.18, 11.58], [12.1, 12.34], [12.34, 12.88], [13.76, 13.76], [13.76, 14.06], [14.06, 14.6], [15.36, 15.48], [15.48, 15.76], [15.76, 16.0]], "isMapOrDoc": false, "personName": null, "portraits": [{"file": "images/portrait_12_0.jpg", "name": "Jimmy Carter", "startFrame": 164, "endFrame": 284, "naturalW": 603, "naturalH": 800}], "overlay": {"cue": "Thirty-three years later, in 1978", "date": "1978", "sub": "THE PRESIDENTIAL UNIT CITATION", "type": "date"}}], "width": 1920, "height": 1080, "gridBg": "grid_bg.mp4", "gridFrames": 301}